From 4cbed92ddd5838242066e015169fd07a33133cd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emanuele Bottelli <bottelliemanuele@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:49:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ui: Save as in the toolbar, and the find field docked beside
 the command search
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two toolbar changes from daily use:

- Save as (file.save_as) gets a button beside Save, worded from the
  command's own label so it needs no new string.
- The find field (⌘F) sits in the toolbar, left of "Find tools and
  commands", instead of floating over the pages: the same controls (count,
  previous, next, options, close), always there; typing into the empty
  field starts a search, Esc ends it and leaves the field empty. The
  floating bar's row became `find_row`/`find_apply`, shared by both.
  Preferences ▸ "Find text in the toolbar" (on by default, persisted as
  `find_in_toolbar`) brings the floating bar back.

The preference label is in every catalog whose coverage test scans the UI
literals (and es, uk, pl, el, te); `persist` sets the new key outside
`json!`, which is at its recursion limit.

Tests: `tests/toolbar_find.rs` (the button, typing into the docked field,
⌘F focusing it, Esc, the preference off, persistence).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
